<p>I originally started writing this based on: “Do we smell nothing as yet of the divine decomposition? Gods, too, decompose. God is dead. God remains dead. And we have killed him.” By Nietzsche in the “Parable of the Madman.”</p>
<p><em><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Overall themes</span></em>: Humanity’s insatiable hunger for progress of knowledge and not worrying about the consequences vs. the reverence required when in the presence of the divine. What if a biologist found the body of god? The first inclination would not be “Let’s worship this,” it would be “Let’s cut this open and see how it ticks.”</p>
<p>This article is followed up by another: <a href="/scp-5512">SCP-5512</a></p>
<p>If you're interested in other works of mine: <a href="/grigori-karpin-s-author-page">Grigori Karpin's Author Page</a></p>
