<p>Well, no you didn’t miss anything I just thought I’d give you some background into my head canon&#8230;</p>
<p>And this is probably a preference thing, so I appreciate not everyone is gonna enjoy my work.</p>
<p>But I absolutely despise when everything is spelled out for me in a story, especially a short story&#8230; horror for me is only catching glimpses, and I think that can work for a contemplative piece as well.</p>
<p>In fact, I wanted much of what you find lacking to be left open to interpretation or filling in by the reader. I wanted someone to read this and ask themselves many of the questions you are contemplating in your critique.</p>
<p>So honestly, it still feels like a success even with your downvote.</p>
<p>Thanks for taking the time to comment, also. No sarcasm, it was legitimately interesting to examine my work through your critiques.</p>

