			<div class="content" id="post-content-4761698">
									

<p>Thank you very much and it’s definitely something I intend to explore in tales and potentially other skips&#8230;</p>
<p>I’ve considered going back in and exploring it further here, but I feel like the taste of knowledge is better for a first “chapter”. Also, I wanted it a bit nebulous re: what 4612-A was doing in these periods, as in my head it was interfering in a lot of ways, both instigating and holding back technological progress. It has its own ideas about how humanity should behave, and like many a bad “parent” it didn’t bother to explain just came in to punish without trying to teach. In many ways that’s why it’s “son” changes his MO by the modern day.</p>
<p>this was very much my first attempt at writing for the wiki, and it shows (at least in my eyes)</p>
<p>Thank you for the kind words :)</p>

